\section{Specify the Interface Before the Datapath}

Build a streaming byte transform \(y=(3a+b)\bmod256\). A transaction is accepted at rising edge \(E_n\) if reset is low and \texttt{vin} is high. Its result and \texttt{vout} are visible immediately after \(E_{n+1}\), provided reset does not intervene. Bubbles travel with the data; when \texttt{vout} is low the receiver ignores the payload. There is no ready signal, so an uninterrupted stream accepts one pair per edge. Reset synchronously cancels both in-flight and outgoing transactions.

Kasprzyk and colleagues' datapath IR makes operands and control predicates explicit together. Here the arithmetic dependency on \(a\) and the need to delay \(b\) are likewise separate from, but coupled to, the predicate \texttt{vin}. The Vienna architecture-description work generates synthesizable HDL and cycle-accurate models from a microarchitecture description; this example instead writes the RTL and an independent reference by hand. In either workflow, generating the RTL is where downstream synthesis begins.

